r is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257rig-k6"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-k6"],"id":"long.record-257rig-k6","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.133 (Uniqueness at a critical crossing)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.133, p. 81, label record:257rig-k6","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For $c\\ge4$, $D$ bounded $[2,c)$, below-half, with genuine crossing deficit $\\tfrac12-\\mathrm{value}(D) < \\ensuremath{w}(c)$:\n$$\nD \\;=\\; \\mathrm{halfGreedyPrefixSupport}(c-1).\n$$\nThus $D=G\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,c-1\\}$: at a critical crossing the support is fixed by $c$. The proof uses the strict inequality between each Mersenne weight and the sum of all later weights, as in Theorem 6.100. Consequently, the support quantifier in Theorem 6.70 does not allow arbitrary choices of $D$. This reduces that hypothesis to a statement about the actual greedy sequence. It does not rule out proving a new bound for that sequence.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257rig-k6","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257rig-k6","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-k6%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_critical_crossing_support_is_greedy_prefix%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-k6%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_critical_crossing_support_is_greedy_prefix%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_critical_crossing